{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21fd7e39d99b57bc5bd3", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Probability - Test 4", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 75, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aab5"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa5d", "title": "Mathematics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9f6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "The probability that a randomly chosen one-one function from the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;to the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;satisfied&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>d</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is"}, "options": [{"id": "a4d774", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9f7"}, {"id": "90a096", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>40</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9f8"}, {"id": "14ab2a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>30</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9f9"}, {"id": "f3e80b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>20</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9fa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9fb", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b450c"], "question": {"text": "A bag contains 19 unbiased coins and one coin with head on both sides. One coin drawn at random is tossed and head turns up. If the probability that the drawn coin was unbiased, is $\\frac{\\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{n}}, \\operatorname{gcd}(\\mathrm{m}, \\mathrm{n})=1$, then $\\mathrm{n}^2-\\mathrm{m}^2$ is equal to :"}, "options": [{"id": "be2a57", "text": "80", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9fc"}, {"id": "aed786", "text": "60", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9fd"}, {"id": "3a21f2", "text": "72", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9fe"}, {"id": "d887c4", "text": "64", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890a9ff"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa00", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b498a"], "concepts": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b4967"], "question": {"text": "A pack of cards has one card missing. Two cards are drawn randomly and are found to be spades. The probability that the missing card is not a spade, is :"}, "options": [{"id": "75ebc7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa01"}, {"id": "3eaeb6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>52</mn><mn>867</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa02"}, {"id": "e0aafc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>39</mn><mn>50</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa03"}, {"id": "2b4966", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>22</mn><mn>425</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa04"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa05", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117af48c5f0702080bdd9b5"], "question": {"text": "Two cards are drawn successively with replacement from a well-shuffled deck of <math><mn>52</mn></math> cards. Let <math><mi>X</mi></math> denote the random variable of number of aces obtained in the two drawn cards. Then <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> equals:"}, "options": [{"id": "aca7c3", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>24</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>169</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa06"}, {"id": "a41e53", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>52</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>169</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa07"}, {"id": "a63e56", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>49</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>169</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa08"}, {"id": "963c27", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>169</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa09"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa0a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["6117b03dc5f0702080bdea7d"], "question": {"text": "Let <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math>, be two events such that the probability that exactly one of them occurs is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>, and the probability that <math><mi>A</mi></math> or <math><mi>B</mi></math>, occurs is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, then the probability of both of them occur together is."}, "options": [{"id": "ca00a3", "text": "<math><mn>0.02</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa0b"}, {"id": "cd572e", "text": "<math><mn>0.20</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa0c"}, {"id": "6519ae", "text": "<math><mn>0.01</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa0d"}, {"id": "6e2d23", "text": "<math><mn>0.10</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa0e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa0f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117afaec5f0702080bde0f1"], "question": {"text": "In a binomial distribution <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, the sum and product of the mean &amp; variance are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math> respectively, then find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is equal to :-"}, "options": [{"id": "d75aa8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>51</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa10"}, {"id": "ca3471", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>52</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa11"}, {"id": "d94708", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>53</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa12"}, {"id": "61cce8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa13"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa14", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b4519"], "question": {"text": "A biased die is marked with numbers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></math>&nbsp;on its faces and the probability of getting a face with mark&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>. If the die is thrown thrice, then the probability, that the sum of the numbers obtained is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn></math>, is"}, "options": [{"id": "e03265", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>11</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa15"}, {"id": "db5472", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>12</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa16"}, {"id": "a7ed47", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa17"}, {"id": "c0fd9c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>13</mn><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>12</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa18"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa19", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b498a"], "concepts": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b4967"], "question": {"text": "There are three bags $X, Y$ and $Z$. Bag $X$ contains 5 one-rupee coins and 4 five-rupee coins; Bag $Y$ contains 4 one-rupee coins and 5 five-rupee coins and Bag Z contains 3 one-rupee coins and 6 five-rupee coins. A bag is selected at random and a coin drawn from it at random is found to be a one-rupee coin. Then the probability, that it came from bag Y, is :"}, "options": [{"id": "3292f3", "text": "$\\frac{1}{4}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa1a"}, {"id": "366d18", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa1b"}, {"id": "d0a66c", "text": "$\\frac{5}{12}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa1c"}, {"id": "04f3d3", "text": "$\\frac{1}{3}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa1d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa1e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "The probability that a randomly chosen <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>- digit number is made from exactly two digits is :"}, "options": [{"id": "fc92f1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>135</mn><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa1f"}, {"id": "36f64a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>150</mn><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa20"}, {"id": "bb07a2", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>134</mn><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa21"}, {"id": "e01679", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>121</mn><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa22"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa23", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b450c"], "question": {"text": "Assume that each born child is equally likely to be a boy or girl. If two families have two children each, then the conditional probability that all children are girls given that at least two are girls is:"}, "options": [{"id": "0445d1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa24"}, {"id": "819242", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa25"}, {"id": "b9ac5a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa26"}, {"id": "746957", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa27"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa28", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117af48c5f0702080bdd9b5"], "question": {"text": "Let a random variable X take values $0,1,2,3$ with $\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=0)=\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=1)=\\mathrm{p}, \\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=2)=\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X}=3)$ and $\\mathrm{E}\\left(\\mathrm{X}^2\\right)=2 \\mathrm{E}(\\mathrm{X})$. Then the value of $8 \\mathrm{p}-1$ is :"}, "options": [{"id": "b0a362", "text": "0", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa29"}, {"id": "0ee27d", "text": "2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa2a"}, {"id": "77b1f4", "text": "1", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa2b"}, {"id": "8ecdbc", "text": "3", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa2c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa2d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b498a"], "concepts": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b4967"], "question": {"text": "A bag contains <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;balls. Two balls are drawn from it at random and both are found to be black. The probability that the bag contains at least <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> black balls is"}, "options": [{"id": "4c0d99", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa2e"}, {"id": "a7e691", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa2f"}, {"id": "6c1013", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa30"}, {"id": "12d40b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa31"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa32", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["6117b03dc5f0702080bdea7d"], "question": {"text": "The coefficients $a, b, c$ in the quadratic equation $a x^2+b x+c=0$ are from the set $\\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\}$. If the probability of this equation having one real root bigger than the other is $p$, then 216 p equals :"}, "options": [{"id": "1b9638", "text": "57", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa33"}, {"id": "269712", "text": "76", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa34"}, {"id": "00441a", "text": "38", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa35"}, {"id": "f68f8f", "text": "19", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa36"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa37", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117afaec5f0702080bde0f1"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> be a random variable such that the probability function of a distribution is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>j</mi></msup></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8734;</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then the mean of the distribution and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>X</mi></math> is positive and even<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;respectively, are:"}, "options": [{"id": "8d4e93", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa38"}, {"id": "c7813b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa39"}, {"id": "ad35ad", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa3a"}, {"id": "c2b1f5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa3b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa3c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b450c"], "question": {"text": "Two integers <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo> </mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo> </mo><mi>y</mi></math> are chosen with replacement from the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>}</mo></math>. Then the probability that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>5</mn></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "60b3cb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>30</mn><mn>121</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa3d"}, {"id": "9e3e24", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>62</mn><mn>121</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa3e"}, {"id": "664823", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>121</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa3f"}, {"id": "59802b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>31</mn><mn>121</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa40"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa41", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b498a"], "concepts": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b4967"], "question": {"text": "In a group of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn></math> people, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>160</mn></math> are smokers and non-vegetarian; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn></math> are smokers and vegetarian and the remaining <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>140</mn></math> are non-smokers and vegetarian. Their chances of getting a particular chest disorder are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>35</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math> respectively. A person is chosen from the group at random and is found to be suffering from the chest disorder. The probability that the selected person is a smoker and non-vegetarian is :"}, "options": [{"id": "819b76", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa42"}, {"id": "668c85", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa43"}, {"id": "436705", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa44"}, {"id": "1d036d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>28</mn><mn>45</mn></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa45"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa46", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "Suppose that <math><mn>20</mn></math> pillars of the same height have been erected along the boundary of circular stadium. If the top of each pillar has been connected by beams with the top of all its non-adjacent pillars, then the total number of beams is:"}, "options": [{"id": "681b13", "text": "<math><mn>170</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa47"}, {"id": "10c1db", "text": "<math><mn>180</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa48"}, {"id": "1eb21b", "text": "<math><mn>210</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa49"}, {"id": "3040aa", "text": "<math><mn>190</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa4a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa4b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117af48c5f0702080bdd9b5"], "question": {"text": "If the probability that the random variable X takes the value $x$ is given by $P(X=x)=k(x+1) 3^{-x}$, $\\mathrm{x}=0,1,2,3 \\ldots \\ldots$, where k is a constant, then $\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{X} \\geq 3)$ is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "8ec82c", "text": "$\\frac{7}{27}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa4c"}, {"id": "2ce074", "text": "$\\frac{4}{9}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa4d"