>E</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa52"}, {"id": "b974fe", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8745;</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa53"}, {"id": "67d709", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8746;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfenced><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa54"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa55", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b498a"], "concepts": ["60e2fafb66f9ce3f243b4967"], "question": {"text": "Three urns A, B and C contain 7 red, 5 black; 5 red, 7 black and 6 red, 6 black balls, respectively. One of the urn is selected at random and a ball is drawn from it. If the ball drawn is black, then the probability that it is drawn from urn $\\mathrm{A}$ is :"}, "options": [{"id": "e06edd", "text": "$\\frac{5}{18}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa56"}, {"id": "1ba399", "text": "$\\frac{5}{16}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa57"}, {"id": "5edb7a", "text": "$\\frac{4}{17}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa58"}, {"id": "65cbb3", "text": "$\\frac{7}{18}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa59"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:42.123Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:42.123Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aab3"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aab1", "title": "Mathematics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa93", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4553"], "concepts": ["60e2faab66f9ce3f243b4519"], "question": {"text": "A bag contains six balls of different colours. Two balls are drawn in succession with replacement. The probability that both the balls are of the same colour is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>. Next four balls are drawn in succession with replacement and the probability that exactly three balls are of the same colours is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><mi>n</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> are co-prime, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></math> is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "615180", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa94"}, {"id": "c00918", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa95"}, {"id": "966e2c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa96"}, {"id": "fea6ef", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa97"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa98", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117afaec5f0702080bde0f1"], "question": {"text": "From a lot of 12 items containing 3 defectives, a sample of 5 items is drawn at random. Let the random variable $\\mathrm{X}$ denote the number of defective items in the sample. Let items in the sample be drawn one by one without replacement. If variance of $X$ is $\\frac{m}{n}$, where $\\operatorname{gcd}(m, n)=1$, then $n-m$ is equal to _________"}, "options": [{"id": "e8a4b6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa99"}, {"id": "fb63c8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa9a"}, {"id": "f0497d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa9b"}, {"id": "b50d79", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa9c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa9d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d5a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb3c66f9ce3f243b4d2a"], "question": {"text": "All five letter words are made using all the letters $\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}, \\mathrm{D}, \\mathrm{E}$ and arranged as in an English dictionary with serial numbers. Let the word at serial number $n$ be denoted by $W_n$. Let the probability $\\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{W}_{\\mathrm{n}}\\right)$ of choosing the word $\\mathrm{W}_{\\mathrm{n}}$ satisfy $\\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{W}_{\\mathrm{n}}\\right)=2 \\mathrm{P}\\left(\\mathrm{W}_{\\mathrm{n}-1}\\right), \\mathrm{n} \\gt 1$.<br/>If $\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{CDBEA})=\\frac{2^\\alpha}{2^\\beta-1}, \\alpha, \\beta \\in \\mathbb{N}$, then $\\alpha+\\beta$ is equal to : _______"}, "options": [{"id": "f39128", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa9e"}, {"id": "218058", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aa9f"}, {"id": "0a1f22", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa0"}, {"id": "1f91b1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df8f"], "concepts": ["6176f3e76581241c70729fbf"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> be the event that the absolute difference between two randomly chosen real numbers in the sample space <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math>, then a is equal to _____ ."}, "options": [{"id": "c67f05", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa3"}, {"id": "4feefe", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa4"}, {"id": "d7c4b1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa5"}, {"id": "254396", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df9c"], "topics": ["6117af49c5f0702080bdda21"], "concepts": ["6117af48c5f0702080bdd9b5"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8230;</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be a sample space of raddom experiment such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>36</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;for every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Then the number of elements in the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8834;</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8805;</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is _____."}, "options": [{"id": "78e5de", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa8"}, {"id": "960592", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaa9"}, {"id": "5710ca", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaaa"}, {"id": "0fe199", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aaab"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:42.216Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:42.216Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f1ac677dc36a890aab4"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:13.638Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:06.975Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d92", "title": "Mathematics", "shortName": "Math"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temp